{"description":"","impact":"The normative document currently claims a frozen version that has been edited twice. A consumer comparing corpus versions cannot tell which 1.3 they hold, and the next release inherits an ambiguous baseline. The gap is structural rather than behavioural: no code reads the corpus version, so nothing fails — which is why it can sit.","acceptanceCriteria":"versioning.md and the shipped corpus version agree about what the two additive section commits were; the sync set (versioning.md, CHANGELOG.md, EKA, exchange.md corpus version, README, vendored pin) is consistent; the EKA index entry for exchange.md names the envelope fields.","context":"Rider: EKA's own index entry for specification/exchange.md still describes the file as (unit, round-trip, package, determinism, version axes) and names no envelope field, so the summary a reader starts from is now thinner than the document.","fixDirection":"Decide one of two, then apply the full sync set in one change: (a) clarification class — add the carve-out sentence to the 1.1 bullet so additive documentation of an already-implemented optional field needs no bump, or (b) additive class — cut 1.4 and touch versioning.md, CHANGELOG.md (new 1.4 section), the EKA version line and version axes, the exchange.md corpus version, the README version table, and re-pin eka-cli/vendored.yaml (EKA bytes are pinned by sha256). Option (a) is cheaper and matches the two commits; option (b) is correct if the standard must be strictly append-only by version. While here, refresh the EKA index topic list for exchange.md.","symptoms":"eka-standard specification/versioning.md states that version 1.3 is frozen and never edited in place, and its 1.1 bullet defines a minor version as backward-compatible normative changes including new sections. Two additive section commits now sit on 1.3 without a bump: c185835 (validity horizon) and 30269b3 (provenance and provenance capture). CONTRIBUTING.md repeats the rule operationally and requires a CHANGELOG entry at the new version. Either the 1.1 bullet needs a clarification carve-out for documenting an already-implemented optional field, or both commits owed a 1.4."}